es, a mobile phone power pack and other essential items.\n\nIf you find yourself outside and hear thunder, protect yourself by finding a safe enclosed shelter (such as a car). Do not shelter under or near trees, or other structures which may be struck by lightning. If you are on an elevated area, move to lower ground.\n\nBe prepared for weather warnings to change quickly: when a weather warning is issued, the Met Office recommends staying up to date with the weather forecast in your area.","language":"en-GB","onset":"2026-08-27T05:00:00+00:00","parameter":[{"value":"2; Yellow; Moderate","valueName":"awareness_level"},{"value":"3; Thunderstorm","valueName":"awareness_type"},{"value":"There is a small chance that homes and businesses could be flooded quickly, with damage to some buildings from floodwater, lightning strikes, hail or strong winds","valueName":"impacts"},{"value":"There is a small chance of fast flowing or deep floodwater causing danger to life","valueName":"impacts"},{"value":"Where flooding or lightning strikes occur, there is a chance of delays and some cancellations to train and bus services","valueName":"impacts"},{"value":"Spray and sudden flooding could lead to difficult driving conditions and some road closures","valueName":"impacts"},{"value":"There is a slight chance that power cuts could occur and other services to some homes and businesses could be lost","valueName":"impacts"},{"value":"There is a small chance that some communities become cut off by flooded roads","valueName":"impacts"}],"responseType":["Prepare"],"senderName":"UK Met Office","severity":"Moderate","urgency":"Future","web":"https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/weather/warnings-and-advice/uk-warnings"}],"msgType":"Alert","scope":"Public","sender":"https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/weather/warnings-and-advice/uk-warnings","sent":"2026-08-25T09:23:16+00:00","source":"2.49.0.0.826.0.GB","status":"Actual"},"raw_properties":{"supersededByAlertId":null,"supersededAt":null,"supersedeType":null,"geometryDescription":"geometry is bbox only, link (member of the feature's links array) with type application/geo+json points to geojson describing the exact shape","geometryType":"bbox","OBJECTID":"138cba25-7018-4dfe-8906-2bb6eb83452e","alertId":"65d9fdf6-8b85-4e9a-bc6a-52a7757d0e0c","countryCode":"UK","featureType":"polygon","hubLanguage":"en-GB","indexArea":0,"indexFeature":0,"indexInfo":0,"hubTime":"2026-08-25T09:23:44Z","hubLink":"https://meteo.fra1.digitaloceanspaces.com/api/archive/warnings/65d9fdf6-8b85-4e9a-bc6a-52a7757d0e0c.xml?AWSAccessKeyId=DO00LYPLJBWUUWC6D6NU&Expires=1787738117&Signature=7aaKoEM7oXGKk69pTiP2EU6temA%3D"}},{"alert_id":"meteo_ebb8438e-91d0-4012-bedb-5c55c2e5fc17","source":"ukmetoffice","title":"Yellow thunderstorm warning","description":"Information on update: Warning area extended further northwestward while removing from parts of East Anglia. A band of heavy showers and thunderstorms is expected to move northwards during this morning. A drier, brighter interlude may follow, but with a chance of further showers and thunderstorms breaking out during the afternoon. Many places will miss these, but where they do occur they may be intense with 20-30 mm rain falling in less than an hour and perhaps 40-50 mm in 2-3 hours in a few spots, leading to some surface water flooding. Large hail and frequent lightning are also possible. The showers and thunderstorms will drift northwards and ease during the evening.\n\nFor further details see https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/weather/warnings-and-advice/uk-warnings","instruction":"Consider if your location is at risk of flash flooding. If so, consider preparing a flood plan and an emergency flood kit.\n\nGive yourself the best chance of avoiding delays by checking road conditions if driving, or bus and train timetables, amending your travel plans if necessary.\n\nPeople cope better with power cuts when they have prepared for them in advance. It's easy to do; consider gathering torches and batteries, a mobile phone power pack and other essential items.\n\nIf you find yourself outside and hear thunder, protect yourself by finding a safe enclosed shelter (such as a car). Do not shelter under or near trees, or other structures which may be struck by lightning. If you are on an elevated area, move to lower ground.\n\nBe prepared for weather warnings to change quickly: when a weather warning is issued, the Met Office recommends staying up to date with the weather forecast in your area.","headline":"A small risk of flooding and disruption from thunderstorms on Wednesday.: UPDATED","area_desc":"East Midlands | East of England | London & South East England | North West England | South West England | Wales | West Midlands | Yorkshire & Humber","severity":"moderate","certainty":"possible","urgency":"immediate","tag":["thunderstorm"],"start_date":"2026-08-26T02:00:00+00:00","end_date":"2026-08-26T21:00:00+00:00","geometry":{"coordinates":[[[-0.2686,51.1654],[-0.3199,51.1629],[-0.3732,51.1632],[-0.4282,51.166],[-0.4847,51.171],[-0.5423,51.1777],[-0.6006,51.1858],[-0.6594,51.1951],[-0.7184,51.2051],[-0.7772,51.2154],[-0.8355,51.2259],[-0.893,51.236],[-0.9494,51.2455],[-1.0043,51.2541],[-1.0575,51.2613],[-1.1023,51.2666],[-1.1464,51.2713],[-1.1898,51.2757],[-1.2327,51.2798],[-1.2751,51.2838],[-1.3171,51.2878],[-1.3587,51.2919],[-1.4001,51.2962],[-1.4413,51.301],[-1.4823,51.3063],[-1.5232,51.3121],[-1.5641,51.3188],[-1.6051,51.3264],[-1.6463,51.3349],[-1.6904,51.3452],[-1.7349,51.3565],[-1.7797,51.3688],[-1.8246,51.3818],[-1.8695,51.3956],[-1.9142,51.41],[-1.9586,51.4248],[-2.0025,51.4399],[-2.0457,51.4553],[-2.0881,51.4708],[-2.1296,51.4862],[-2.1699,51.5016],[-2.2089,51.5166],[-2.2465,51.5313],[-2.2761,51.5431],[-2.3045,51.5546],[-2.3319,51.5659],[-2.3583,51.5772],[-2.3841,51.5884],[-2.4094,51.5998],[-2.4343,51.6112],[-2.459,51.6229],[-2.4837,51.6349],[-2.5085,51.6472],[-2.5337,51.66],[-2.5594,51.6734],[-2.5857,51.6873],[-2.6129,51.7019],[-2.6487,51.7215],[-2.6849,51.7417],[-2.7215,5